 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A presentation helps share information clearly: a project report, a health talk, a club announcement.\nSteps:\n1. Plan: the aim, the audience and the main points (one idea per slide).\n2. Create slides: a title slide, content slides, a conclusion and a thank-you slide.\n3. Add pictures, charts or diagrams that support the message.\n4. Apply a theme; use few transitions and animations.\n5. Check spelling; rehearse with speaker notes; present in slide show view.\nGood design rules:\n• few words: short bullet points (about 6 lines of about 6 words);\n• large, clear fonts (at least 24 points for text);\n• high contrast between text and background;\n• do not read the slides word for word; look at the audience.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "x": "a slide with ten long sentences in small writing"
  },
  "problem": "What is wrong with {x}, and how can it be improved?",
  "steps": [
   "The audience cannot read small writing, and long sentences are boring.",
   "Use a few short bullet points in a large font, and say the details aloud."
  ],
  "answer": "Too much small text: use short bullet points in a large font.",
  "checks": []
 },
